course: dictionary
lesson: 14244
title: Negate: cancel out or say no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To negate something means to cancel it out, so it has no effect. «The rain negated our picnic plans» means the rain cancelled the picnic, so it did not happen. Two things pull against each other, and one wins by undoing the other.
explain: Negate can also mean to say something is not true. «The judge negated the witness's story» means the judge said the story was not true. This is a formal word, so you will meet it in serious writing and exams.
explain: In grammar, to negate a sentence is to make it negative, usually by adding «not» or «don't». «I like peas» becomes «I don't like peas». Check it: the meaning flips from yes to no. In maths, negating a number gives its opposite: 5 becomes -5.
fact: Negate is a verb: negate, negates, negated, negating.
fact: «Negate» means to cancel something out, or to make it have no effect.
fact: «Negate» also means to deny something or say that it is not true.
fact: To negate a sentence means to make it negative, often by adding «not».
fact: In maths, negating 5 gives -5, which is its opposite.
exercise: «The cold weather negated our plan for a picnic.» What does negated mean here? | Repeated the picnic plan | *Cancelled, so the picnic did not happen | Hid the picnic food | Made the picnic bigger
exercise: Mia says her brother's idea is wrong, and «she negated what he said». What does negated mean? | *Said it was not true | Agreed with it loudly | Wrote it down neatly | Forgot it straight away
exercise: Change «I like peas» into a negative sentence. | Peas, I like them | I like peas very much | I really liked peas | *I don't like peas
test: «Eating too much sugar can negate the good effects of a healthy meal.» What does negate mean here? | Repeat the meal | *Cancel out, so the good effect is lost | Share the meal with friends | Make the meal taste nicer
test: Negating the number 8 gives what? | 80 | 0 | *-8 | 8
exam: Which sentence is the negative of «She can swim»? | She can swim too | She swam yesterday | Can she swim? | *She can't swim
